# beatmania IIDX 3rd style (GC992 VER. JAB), Konami 2000: as bmiidx3-boot.his, whose game it is a revision or a sibling of.
# beatmania IIDX 3rd style (Twinkle): first power-on from blank NVRAM. The BIOS boots the
# program CD over SCSI; the SPU board loads the hard disk into wave RAM; the device check
# passes everything but the backup RAM (RTC XRAM): E150 BACKUP DATA ERROR by frame ~1500,
# then "1P START = BACKUP CLEAR" (by ~2100). 1P Start clears it and the game goes on
# towards attract. Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, to compare
# HIRAKU's Twinkle core with MAME (PLAN.md section 21, TW-0).
game bmiidx3b

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 2400 press "1 Player Start" 8
from 0 every 60 snap
at 9000 quit
